{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review gate: first local run graded a STALE plan — cause identified, re-run in flight\n\n`rebar review-plan` now completes locally (the Bedrock provider is present in the worktree venv),\nand the LLM layer ran for the first time: `coverage.llm_ran: true`, `source: attested`,\n`verified_at_sha: 1a589bdfc2a882f09160530655f06077764b33d8`. Verdict **BLOCK**, 2 blocking +\n4 advisory, unsigned (`signature: {\"signed\": false, \"reason\": \"BLOCK\"}`).\n\n**But it reviewed a superseded copy of the plan, and I checked rather than assumed.** Both\nblocking findings quote description text I had already replaced:\n\n> `AC2: '(fsck could not run, rc not in 0|1) remains distinguishable'`\n> `Note: 'an uninitialised store also exits 1, not 2 ... the exact discriminator used instead'`\n\nNeither string exists in the current description. The cause is a **store divergence between the\nMCP server's clone and this checkout's `.tickets-tracker`**, and it is reproducible:\n\n```\n# same ticket, same moment, two clones:\nMCP show_ticket        -> 'Two commands, two contracts' present   (v3)\nCLI rebar show (local) -> 'rc not in 0|1' present                 (v2, superseded)\n```\n\nThe v3 description edit's push had been REJECTED minutes earlier —\n`push_status: {state: \"final-push-rejected\", detail: \"! [rejected] HEAD -> tickets (fetch first)\",\nunpushed: 6}` — ordinary busy-ref contention on a shared store. The local CLI clone was pulling\ncorrectly (its tracker HEAD advanced `87dac76bab -> 221b6e6131` while I watched), it simply had\nnothing to pull yet. A later MCP write returned `push_status: ok`, and ~20s after that the local\nclone converged:\n\n```\nv3 present: True | old AC2 rc-band present: False\nfile_impact includes coverage test: True | comments: 9\n```\n\nSo the two blocking findings are a **timing artifact, not plan defects**. I have re-run\n`review-plan` against the converged plan and will record that verdict when it lands. Recording\nthe mechanism because a stale-plan BLOCK is indistinguishable from a real one unless you diff\nthe quoted text against the live description — worth knowing on any busy multi-agent store.\n\n### The advisories, however, included a REAL gap — fixed\n\n`project.symbol-reference-completeness` (validity 1.0) caught that the plan's file inventory\nomitted `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py`, where `fsck` is classified\nin `EXEMPT_GENERIC` **by a string dict key** — invisible to the LSP, exactly the Serena blind spot\n`docs/code-navigation.md` documents. The code change was already correct (I had moved it to\n`CANONICAL` in the first pass), but the declared `file_impact` did not name it, so the gate was\nright that the plan under-declared its blast radius.\n\n`file_impact` corrected to match the commit exactly — 13 entries, now including\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py` and `docs/output-schemas.md`, and\nwith the two entries that never materialised removed (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_outputs.py`\npasses unchanged; `docs/mcp-reference.md` regenerates to a no-op because the tool's docstring did\nnot change). Verified against `git show --name-only HEAD` + working tree.\n\nTwo other advisories were already-fixed text from the same stale copy:\n- the recover/`_transform_json` finding (validity 0.9) — this is the reviewed blocker, and its\n  `suggested_fix` independently proposes the exact design I had already implemented: *\"Split\n  fsck_report into a scan reader … and a recover reader that returns {mode:'recover',\n  report:<narrative verbatim>, issues:[], fixed:[], issue_count:0, returncode} without passing\n  through _transform_json; add a `mode` discriminator to FsckOut/the schema.\"* Useful\n  corroboration from an independent reviewer that the chosen representation is the right one.\n- `E2` underspecified-oracle on AC2 — v3 states the discriminator inline in the\n  \"Two commands, two contracts\" table and in Plan step 1, rather than deferring it to a comment.\n\n### One advisory deliberately NOT actioned\n\n`P6 ac-quality` (DET, minor, impact 0.4): *\"vague/subjective terms present: sufficient\"*. The\nonly occurrence is in the operator-authored LIVE VALIDATION criterion — *\"A passing local test is\nNOT sufficient\"* — where the word is a **negation tightening** the requirement, not a vague\nacceptance threshold. Rewording an operator-specified close condition to satisfy a keyword scan\nwould weaken the thing it is there to enforce. Left as written, flagged here so the decision is\nvisible rather than silently ignored.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787876384139778540,"uuid":"d28bb439-9db2-4ae9-b2b4-32d5fa2cd46e"}